ZERO / EZERO 0.11.0 — NATIVE linux X64 TOOLKIT

The compiler, Ezero runtime, setup tool, updater, SHA256 and UEFI loader are
original Zero programs. The toolkit needs no shell script, Python, CMD,
PowerShell, external compiler or foreign language runtime. Keep lib/ beside
the native zero and ezero commands. Linux uses direct Linux syscalls;
Windows uses Windows operating-system APIs. Windows execution verification
uses Wine; this is not a claim of testing on a native Windows installation.

On Linux, run ./zero and ./ezero. On Windows, run zero.exe and ezero.exe.
Paths with spaces use the normal quoting rules of the invoking terminal.

    zero examples/hello.zero hello
    ezero examples/banana.ezero banana
    zero --help

Default output matches the host platform. Windows output names usually end
in .exe. Explicit targets include --host, --windows, --efi, --efi32, --real,
--raw, --raw32, --app64 and --app32. Other targets need their own execution
environment. Existing output paths are refused. Compilation runs our own
compiler/frontend/packer applications in process, without a subprocess.

Ezero provides unquoted text, inferred numeric values, lists indexed from 1,
functions and automatic memory management. lines(text) splits text into lines;
join(text_list | separator) combines text values. Host-file conveniences are
readfile, writefile (new files only), fileexists, arguments and host. See the
language/API documents and examples for exact size and type rules.

Prepare ISO/storage files in a new directory:
    zero-setup prepare zero.iso NEW_DIRECTORY
    zero-setup status NEW_DIRECTORY
    zero-setup remove NEW_DIRECTORY

Deploy the supplied own UEFI x64 loader alongside the ISO:
    zero-setup deploy zero.iso ZEROX64.EFI NEW_DIRECTORY

The deployed loader reads system.iso from its own directory through firmware
file services. To boot it, that directory must be on a filesystem the firmware
can read (normally FAT), and the firmware must launch ZEROX64.EFI. Deploy does
not format a partition or register a firmware/Windows/Linux boot-menu entry.
An arbitrary NTFS/ext4/Btrfs host folder is not automatically bootable.
storage.data is prepared ZeroFS content, not a file-backed live OS disk.
See source/installer/README.txt and source/installer/boot/README.txt.

Local update preparation:
    zero-update init zero.iso 1 NEW_STORE
    zero-update publish next-zero.iso 2 NEW_INBOX
    zero-update check NEW_INBOX NEW_STORE
    zero-update status NEW_STORE
    zero-update verify NEW_STORE
    zero-update rollback NEW_STORE

Release counters start at 1. Local preparation does not activate the booted
OS. There is no Internet release server, publisher signature or TLS transport.
Use trusted local releases. See source/updater/README.txt for periodic local
checks, recovery commands, locking and exact persistence limitations.

Rebuild from included original source with the same native tool:
    zero source/compiler.zero rebuilt-compiler
    zero source/compiler-cli.zero rebuilt-command
    zero source/installer/setup.zero rebuilt-setup
    zero source/installer/boot/loader.zero rebuilt-loader.efi --efi
    zero source/updater/update.zero rebuilt-update

The direct stream compiler reference is source/compiler-seed (or .exe).
SHA256SUMS.txt covers every package file; BUILD-INPUTS.sha256 records source
inputs. zero-sha256 computes SHA256 without an external hash program.
The ISO is distributed separately; these archives contain no disk images.
